message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-11-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of the surgical team. You were admitted last night with left upper quadrant pain. Can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-11-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started about a week ago. It’s sharp, under my left rib, and goes around to my back. It gets much worse when I eat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-11-10 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Is this different from your usual pain from the ulcers you’ve had before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-11-10 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, before it was more in the middle, near my stomach. This feels higher and sharper."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-11-10 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You’re on a G-tube for feeding—any issues with that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-11-10 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "There’s been a little drainage around the tube for a few weeks, but it’s not painful. The feeds sometimes cause discomfort, but not as bad as eating by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-11-10 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check that. For now, we’re keeping you on bowel rest—no food or tube feeds—just IV fluids. We’ll do some tests to find the cause."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-11-10 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Should I stop my regular meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-11-10 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, we’ll keep your pantoprazole, sucralfate, and other meds. We’re giving IV fluids with vitamins and pain control as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-11-10 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an X-ray and a contrast study through your G-tube. No signs of a leak or blockage. Your pain isn’t from a perforation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-11-10 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. So what’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-11-10 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning an EGD—upper endoscopy—tomorrow to look at your stomach and bypass connections. That should show if there’s an ulcer or other issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-11-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick update—we’re still reviewing your labs. White count is normal, no infection signs. We’ll proceed with the EGD tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-11-11 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any idea why the pain started suddenly?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-11-11 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be a new ulcer or irritation from stomach acid. The EGD will help confirm that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-11-12 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from the EGD. We found a small 10 mm ulcer at the gastrojejunal anastomosis—the connection from your stomach pouch to the intestine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-11-12 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why I’m in so much pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-11-12 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s likely the cause. The rest of the intestine looked normal. We’ll start you on IV pantoprazole to reduce acid and help it heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-11-12 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I restart my tube feeds now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-11-12 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll try. We’re starting at your usual rate—110 mL/hr cycled. Let us know if it causes pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-11-12 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You mentioned increased pain with the feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-11-12 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s worse, especially after the cycle starts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-11-12 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll switch to continuous feeding at half the rate—55 mL/hr—to see if that helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-11-13 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still some discomfort with continuous feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-11-13 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, not as bad, but still there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-11-13 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching to a more concentrated formula at 30 mL/hr. It delivers the same calories with less volume, which may reduce irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-11-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re progressing your diet to bariatric stage 5—soft foods. Try small amounts and let us know if it hurts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-11-14 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I tried some mashed potatoes, but the pain came back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-11-14 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, we’ll hold oral intake for now. The tube feeds aren’t helping much either, so we’re stopping them today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-11-14 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Then how will I get nutrition?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-11-14 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll place a PICC line tomorrow to start TPN—total parenteral nutrition—through your vein. It will give you all the nutrients you need."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-11-15 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to do a CT scan to make sure there’s no blockage or fistula causing the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-11-15 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it show the ulcer too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-11-15 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "CT doesn’t show ulcers well, but it checks for complications like leaks or obstructions. The EGD already confirmed the ulcer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-11-15 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT is back. No obstruction, no fistula, no free air. Good news. But we noticed a small pustule near your G-tube site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-11-15 20:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s been a little red, but not painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-11-15 20:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We drained it and sent a culture. It may be MRSA, so we’ll start antibiotics just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-11-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your PICC line was placed this morning. We’re starting TPN. You’ll get all your nutrition through the line now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-11-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be on this long?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-11-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Only until the ulcer heals and we can safely restart tube feeds. We’ll monitor closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-11-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The culture came back: MRSA. We’re continuing the antibiotic. The redness isn’t spreading, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-11-17 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-11-17 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. It’s localized. We’re treating it, and you’re not running a fever, so it’s under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-11-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to try restarting tube feeds tomorrow. The ulcer should be healing, and we need to get off TPN if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-11-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if it hurts again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2170-11-19 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start slow. We’re switching to Peptamen Bariatric—a pre-digested formula. It’s easier to tolerate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2170-11-20 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on Peptamen for a day. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2170-11-20 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. The pain is less, especially during the day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2170-11-20 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re increasing to a cycled rate of 60 mL/hr. If you tolerate this, we can plan for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2170-11-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Pain is minimal, you’re tolerating feeds, and your labs are stable. We’ll remove the PICC tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2170-11-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2170-11-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely tomorrow. You’ll go home on liquid pantoprazole twice a day, sucralfate, and your other meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2170-11-21 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the nortriptyline? I saw it was increased."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2170-11-21 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, to 50 mg at night for pain control. Please let your psychiatrist know about the change."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2170-11-21 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The PICC is out. You’re now fully on tube feeds and tolerating them. We’ll finalize your discharge plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2170-11-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home today. Continue Peptamen at 60 mL/hr for 12 hours, flush the tube as instructed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2170-11-22 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if the pain comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2170-11-22 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use the hydromorphone as needed. Call if pain worsens, or if you develop fever, vomiting, or black stools."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2170-11-22 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the G-tube site?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2170-11-22 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Wash with soap and water. No dressing needed if no drainage. Call if it becomes red, swollen, or painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2170-11-22 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2170-11-22 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your gastroenterologist in one week, surgeon in three. Keep all your other appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2170-11-22 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2170-11-22 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Rest well, take your meds, and call if anything concerns you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2170-11-22 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you understand not to take NSAIDs like ibuprofen or naproxen. They can cause ulcers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2170-11-22 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ll stick to acetaminophen if I need pain relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2170-11-22 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Also, avoid driving while on the hydromorphone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2170-11-22 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll have someone help at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2170-11-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—we added docusate and senna for constipation. You had a lot of stool on the CT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2170-11-22 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been a bit backed up. Thanks for catching that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2170-11-22 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send the discharge summary to your providers. You’re all set to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2170-11-22 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad this is over. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2170-11-22 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2170-11-22 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check—any last questions before discharge?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2170-11-22 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got it all. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2170-11-22 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright. The transport team will take you out shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2170-11-22 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One quick update—your wound culture confirmed MRSA, but it was localized and treated. No further action needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2170-11-22 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2170-11-22 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We monitored it closely. You’re fine now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2170-11-22 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Discharge papers are ready. Nurse will go over meds and feeding instructions one more time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2170-11-22 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll review them carefully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2170-11-22 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re discharging you home with services. A nurse will check in on your G-tube care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2170-11-22 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2170-11-22 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2170-11-22 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final note: your pain service increased nortriptyline to help with chronic pain. Monitor for drowsiness."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-11-10 00:19:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-11-22 17:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for left upper quadrant abdominal pain worsened by oral and tube feeding intake, different from prior ulcer episodes. After bowel rest and imaging, an EGD revealed a 10 mm gastrojejunal anastomotic ulcer. Initial tube feeding adjustments caused persistent pain, leading to discontinuation and initiation of TPN via PICC on hospital day 7. A small MRSA-positive pustule at the G-tube site was drained and treated. Feeds were retrialed on hospital day 12 with Peptamen Bariatric formula at a cycled rate of 60 mL/hr, which was well tolerated. The PICC was removed, and the patient was discharged home on enteral feeds, liquid pantoprazole twice daily, sucralfate, and an increased nortriptyline dose for pain. Follow-up was arranged with gastroenterology and surgery.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastrojejunal ulcer, unspecified as acute or chronic, without mention of hemorrhage or perforation, without mention of obstruction",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Polycystic ovaries",
      "Methicillin resistant Staphylococcus aureus in conditions classified elsewhere and of unspecified site",
      "Unspecified local infection of skin and subcutaneous tissue",
      "Gastrostomy status"
    ]
  }
}
